# Keep the code graph about the CODE (TODO J8.3, fixes J0.3 / J6.1 / much of J2).
#
# Measured on the 2026-08-09 graph before this file existed: bench/ was 1043 of 3729 nodes (28%),
# 1858 of 6809 edges (27%), and DOMINATED 93 of 293 communities (32%). That is a third of the
# clustering budget spent on scaffolding, and it is why every "Surprising Connections" entry in
# the report was a bench/* -> src/* edge — a test file importing the code it tests, which is the
# least surprising edge in any codebase.
#
# THE TRADE, stated plainly so nobody rediscovers it as a bug: the graph can no longer answer
# "which test covers X". That is an acceptable loss here only because this repo names tests after
# their subject (bench/test_<topic>.py), so a glob answers it as well as a graph would.
#
# To build a FULL graph including tests, move this file aside for the run:
#   mv .graphifyignore .graphifyignore.off && graphify update . --force && mv .graphifyignore.off .graphifyignore
bench/
